# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# Item 738 slice 2: a captured Structure's value field as a call argument (`twice(loc\value)`) is read
# through the copy's table like any read: 2 * 40 + 2.  Success is 7.
Model:
    int: other 5
    int: value 0
end: Model

fn: twice (int: v) int
    return: v + v

fn: makeReader (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    loc: merge Model
    loc\value: n
    fn: read (int: x) int
        return: twice(loc\value) + x
    return: read

@: r40 makeReader(40)
int: a (r40: 2)
int: ok 7
if: a != 82
    ok: 1
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
